// A whole number divided by nought is 0 with nothing left, and the least
// number by -1 is itself with nothing left: the same on one core, many
// and the GPU (and on every processor: the instruction alone stops the
// program on x86-64 and gives a number on arm64).
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/divide_nought.ent | FileCheck %s
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/divide_nought.ent | FileCheck %s

// CHECK: 0 0 0 0 0 0
// CHECK-NEXT: -2147483648 0 -9223372036854775808 0 571428571 3
// CHECK-NEXT: -3 -1 -3 1 3 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 0 0 -5 0 0 0
